  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when you've invested in beautiful marble for your bathroom, only to find it looking less than stellar after installation. Often, a dull appearance can be traced back to a few key areas in the installation process. One common culprit is skipping the proper sealing steps. Marble is porous, meaning it can absorb liquids and dulling agents if not properly sealed after installation. Another issue could be the type of thin-set or grout used; sometimes, if a non-white or staining product is used, it can bleed into the marble and affect its appearance. Also, rushing the cure time for adhesives and grout before sealing can lead to issues. These materials need to fully dry and cure to ensure the marble's integrity and appearance are maintained. A professional will ensure the right, non-staining materials are used, and that proper cure and sealing times are observed. Getting a professional involved ensures you get that gorgeous, long-lasting finish you’re expecting.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}